WEBVTT

00:07:29.956 --> 00:07:33.556
Surely if you want to find
something that's missing,

00:07:33.596 --> 00:07:37.196
that's the general approach
you have to take, right?

00:07:38.196 --> 00:07:39.356
Wrong.

00:07:41.276 --> 00:07:45.436
We actually just have to accept the fact
that these missing particles

00:07:45.476 --> 00:07:48.436
are not going to interact
with our detectors,

00:07:48.476 --> 00:07:49.916
whatever we do.

00:07:52.156 --> 00:07:54.036
But that's not game over.

00:07:56.156 --> 00:07:58.156
In the same way that I didn't give up

00:07:58.156 --> 00:08:02.076
on being able to do
laboratory experiments myself,